<header class="board-head"><div><h1>Ken Hawkins / four design studies</h1><p class="board-intro">Japanese Mega Drive packaging → a personal publishing system. November 2026.</p></div><span class="board-intro">EXPLORATIONS / 01—04</span></header>
<div class="tools" aria-label="Choose a design"><input type="radio" name="direction" id="choice-hybrid" checked><label for="choice-hybrid">04 / Cartridge + signal</label><input type="radio" name="direction" id="choice-cartridge"><label for="choice-cartridge">01 / Cartridge</label><input type="radio" name="direction" id="choice-editorial"><label for="choice-editorial">02 / Graphic press</label><input type="radio" name="direction" id="choice-signal"><label for="choice-signal">03 / Signal blue</label><div class="size-tools"><input type="radio" name="size" id="size-wide" checked><label for="size-wide">Wide</label><input type="radio" name="size" id="size-phone"><label for="size-phone">Phone</label></div></div>
<p class="rationale" id="note-cartridge"><strong>01 / Cartridge.</strong> Closest to your reference: cream paper, yellow disc, tilted black typography, cobalt and vermilion. The case study becomes the cover sticker; the writing lives in a clean blue register.</p>
<p class="rationale" id="note-editorial"><strong>02 / Graphic press.</strong> The packaging’s typographic collision meets your newspaper and information-design background. Huge name, editorial folios, one yellow masthead. The strongest foundation for a long-lived publishing system.</p><p class="rationale" id="note-signal"><strong>03 / Signal blue.</strong> A more technical interpretation: cobalt sleeve, orbital geometry, red information strip and a cream reading surface. The energy comes from scale and contrast; the writing stays calm.</p><p class="rationale" id="note-hybrid"><strong>04 / Cartridge + signal.</strong> Your selected direction: option 1’s cream paper, yellow disc, angled typography and colour blocks, with option 3’s “Make it make sense” and “Platforms. Content. People. Connected by design.” The three original studies remain for comparison.</p><div class="viewport" id="viewport">
