</div><p class="board-intro" style="margin-top:18px">Direction studies: display copy and article summaries are exploratory. Navigation links point to the existing site. No Sonic characters or SEGA marks are used.</p>
<details style="margin-top:20px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6"><summary>Research notes &amp; sources</summary><p>Reference: Japanese Sonic the Hedgehog Mega Drive packaging, released 26 July 1991 (<a href="https://sonic.sega.jp/SonicChannel/gametitle/SonicTheHedgehog.html">SEGA title record</a>). The supplied cover gives us cream paper, a yellow disc, compressed black type, diagonal fields and sparse geometric marks.</p><p>Related visual languages: <a href="https://www.vam.ac.uk/collections/postmodernism">postmodern design / Memphis (V&amp;A)</a> and <a href="https://eyeondesign.aiga.org/april-greiman-is-still-ahead-of-the-curve/">New Wave typography / April Greiman (AIGA)</a>. These are visual affinities, not a claim of documented direct influence on the Sonic cover.</p><p>The proposals preserve upright, readable body text and use expressive type for display. They use original geometric graphics and English captions. Overall packaging authorship has not been established from a primary source.</p></details></main></body></html>